The complete former kernel agrees with the new cached implementation over
multiple stage counts and seeded angles on this toolchain. The former report's
normalization loop agrees with every recorded coordinate of the twelve-step
example. The result-only and traced APIs share the same recurrence and final
compensation; extra trace normalization does not change the result.

> Finite-stage error and the floating floor

In ideal real arithmetic the unit direction has angle φ−z_N. For N≥1,
|z_N|≤α_(N−1) follows by induction. The first step maps |φ|≤π/2 to
|z₁|≤π/4=α₀. If |zᵢ|≤α_(i−1), the next magnitude is
||zᵢ|−αᵢ|. Concavity of atan gives α_(i−1)≤2αᵢ, so that magnitude is at
most αᵢ. Sine and cosine are one-Lipschitz, giving an ideal per-component
truncation bound α_(N−1), approximately 2^(1−N) radians.

This bound assumes exact rotation arithmetic, exact constants and exact gain
compensation relative to the reduced target. It does not bound all rounding or
input-period reduction errors of the floating program. Small residual and small
unit-norm defect also do not certify the direction for a huge original angle.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cordic_error.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto grid=dm::seql(-10,10,2001);
  const std::vector<double> angles(grid.begin(),grid.end());
  const auto rows=dm::algorithms::cordic_error_sweep(angles,{0,1,2,4,8,12,20,32,40,44,52,64});
  std::vector<double> n,error,bound_n,bound;
  std::print("| stages N | original angles | max sine error | max cosine error | max norm defect | first worst angle |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& r:rows) {
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.3e} | {:.3e} | {:.3e} | {:.6f} |\n",r.iterations,r.samples,r.max_sin_error,r.max_cos_error,r.max_norm_error,r.worst_angle);
    n.push_back(r.iterations);error.push_back(std::log10(std::max(r.max_component_error,1e-20)));
    if(r.iterations) {
      bound_n.push_back(r.iterations);
      bound.push_back(std::log10(std::atan(std::ldexp(1.,1-r.iterations))));
    }
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(n,error,"measured max",{37,99,235},2).points(n,error,"",{37,99,235},4)
      .line(bound_n,bound,"ideal bound",{220,38,38},1.5)
      .legend({"measured max","ideal bound"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}})
      .title("More rotations meet a binary64 rounding floor")
      .x_label("requested circular stages N").y_label("log10 component error; display floor 1e-20")
      .y_limits(-21,1).size(900,560).save_svg("build/cordic_error.svg");
}
```
